From: Phil Taylor <phil@m0vse.uk>
Subject: [PATCH 0153] mac80211: validate transmit queue id

Carry upstream 7ce2f118a2389e8f0a64068c6fe7cc7d40639be0 on the selected 6.18.7
backports without a baseline change. Preserve upstream authorship and
sign-offs; hardware acceptance remains separate from offline validation.

Signed-off-by: Phil Taylor <phil@m0vse.uk>
---
diff --git a/package/kernel/mac80211/patches/ath9k/952-wifi-validate-transmit-queue-id.patch b/package/kernel/mac80211/patches/ath9k/952-wifi-validate-transmit-queue-id.patch
new file mode 100644
--- /dev/null
+++ b/package/kernel/mac80211/patches/ath9k/952-wifi-validate-transmit-queue-id.patch
@@ -0,0 +1,40 @@
+From 7ce2f118a2389e8f0a64068c6fe7cc7d40639be0 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
+From: Tristan Madani <tristan@talencesecurity.com>
+Date: Wed, 15 Apr 2026 22:23:43 +0000
+Subject: [PATCH] wifi: ath9k: fix OOB access from firmware tx status queue ID
+MIME-Version: 1.0
+Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
+Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit
+
+ath_tx_edma_tasklet() accesses sc->tx.txq[ts.qid] where ts.qid is a
+4-bit hardware field (0-15), but the txq array only has
+ATH9K_NUM_TX_QUEUES (10) entries. A qid >= 10 causes an OOB array
+access.
+
+Add a bounds check on ts.qid before using it as an array index.
+
+Fixes: fce041beb03f ("ath9k: unify edma and non-edma tx code, improve tx fifo handling")
+Signed-off-by: Tristan Madani <tristan@talencesecurity.com>
+Acked-by: Toke Høiland-Jørgensen <toke@toke.dk>
+Link: https://patch.msgid.link/20260415222343.1540564-1-tristmd@gmail.com
+Signed-off-by: Jeff Johnson <jeff.johnson@oss.qualcomm.com>
+---
+ drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath9k/xmit.c | 5 +++++
+ 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+)
+
+diff --git a/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath9k/xmit.c b/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath9k/xmit.c
+index 4a0f465aa2fe50..89d8b31787846b 100644
+--- a/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath9k/xmit.c
++++ b/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath9k/xmit.c
+@@ -2744,6 +2744,11 @@ void ath_tx_edma_tasklet(struct ath_softc *sc)
+ 			continue;
+ 		}
+ 
++		if (ts.qid >= ATH9K_NUM_TX_QUEUES) {
++			ath_dbg(common, XMIT, "invalid qid %d\n", ts.qid);
++			continue;
++		}
++
+ 		txq = &sc->tx.txq[ts.qid];
+ 
+ 		ath_txq_lock(sc, txq);
